Add ONE line to your globals.css, immediately after the tailwind import:

    @import "tailwindcss";
    @import "../styles/jhai-theme-base.css";

Adjust the relative path to wherever the file landed. To rebrand, append a :root block AFTER that import overriding only --jh-* values — see the CLIENT REBRAND block at the foot of the file.

The shadcn semantic tokens (--background, --foreground, --primary, --border and the rest) are NOT in that CSS file. They arrive as cssVars, which the CLI merges into your project's own :root block. That is deliberate: your :root is declared later in globals.css than the @import, so a mapping inside the file would render correctly on a bare project and silently lose on a real shadcn one.

Do not edit any --ink-*, --paper-*, --bjarmi-* or shadcn semantic token directly. They resolve through --jh-* and editing them breaks the chain.

WHY type IS registry:theme AND NOT registry:base — measured, shadcn CLI 4.21.0. A registry:base item's cssVars block is silently ignored: the files land, the CLI reports success, and not one token reaches globals.css. registry:theme applies them correctly. There is no error and no warning, so this is only visible by diffing globals.css after an install.
